# Integration tests

Middle of the pyramid: verify **contracts between components**, not every branch.

## What belongs here

- FastAPI routes via `TestClient` (ASGI in-process)
- Router → service wiring with **mocked** `LLMService` / provider SDK
- OpenAPI path presence, status codes (200 / 422 / 502), response shape
- Config lifespan fail-fast when keys missing (if tested without full process)

## Rules

- Test **one boundary at a time** (e.g. HTTP ↔ service), not the whole production stack
- Prefer real framework pieces (FastAPI, Pydantic) + fake LLM over mocking everything
- Keep tests deterministic; mock provider HTTP, do not call OpenAI/Anthropic
- Fewer than unit tests; cover happy path + main failure contracts (422, 502)
- Still automated and CI-friendly (seconds, not minutes)

## Example targets in this repo

- `GET /health` → 200 `{"status":"ok"}`
- `POST /api/v1/estimate` valid body → 200 with mocked estimation
- `POST /api/v1/estimate` short/missing body → 422
- Provider exception → 502 `LLM provider error: ...`

## Do not

- Re-test every pure validator branch already covered in unit tests
- Require a running Docker container (that is e2e / CI smoke)
- Assert on full Markdown prose of the model — assert structure/metadata
